 "q-35789/selection/4604fcc65c5a4967de66b95824681642ba82c9d6b06268ae432e08b625deb692" "q-35789/selection/bb141fa0e297d693d9af83c7a98a8e80d29cb6a91b8b6ec4a29067a9d803e3bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35789" :question/id #uuid "b15112f4-7893-524a-8de9-46c29499aff4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35789" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35789/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35789"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135442/selection/154e475ce1d0b228e9b825a30ceced0d5bb4b9f2e002b21fbe6c42819912a9bc" :answer/id #uuid "bc7583a4-a122-5d76-98f6-f23eafa3fa27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.29 \\\\ 0.43 \\\\ 0.28\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135442/selection/ccc5009658c5b0cd3797d8c11e7a0c1e2d7baa2197b295eada4bc900fedbd315" :answer/id #uuid "1818f